# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Godot engine cache
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated from source every time the project is opened: the import cache
# (.godot/imported), shader cache, per-user editor layout and folding state.
# ~800 MB of it, and it churns on every headless run or engine patch bump.
# The *.import files next to each asset ARE committed — those are the settings;
# .godot/ is just the compiled result of applying them.
/.godot/

# Written by the export dialog. Empty today, but this is where Godot stores the
# script encryption key and the codesigning identity password — never commit it.
export_credentials.cfg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gdre_tools decompiler leftovers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Godot skips directories whose name starts with "." when it scans res://, so
# none of this is part of the game — it is the decompiler's working output kept
# alongside the recovered project. Nothing in the project references it.
#   .assets/        original .fbx/.blend sources extracted from the pck
#   .autoconverted/ .gdc bytecode dumps of the original scripts
/.assets/
/.autoconverted/
gdre_export.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The exported mod .pck is a build artifact and would blow past GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file limit anyway — ship it as a Release asset instead.
*.pck
*.pck.bak
/build/
/export/
/exports/

# Godot Android build template (only present if you ever install it)
/android/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Windows System Restore / antivirus shadow copies, e.g.
# ~libgodotsteam.windows.template_debug.x86_64.dll~RF251057.TMP left beside the
# GodotSteam binaries. Never yours, never wanted.
*.TMP
~*.tmp
